## Task done

`autoscaling-viz__task3-panel6-redesign.md` is complete -- the last queued task in the sequenced
review-fix series (bugfix-cluster -> panel3-redesign -> panel6-redesign). Commit `3f12aaa1` on
`autoscaling-viz` (tip; was `08927557`). Implements
`planning/autoscaling-viz-panel6-redesign-plan.md` in full: extractor extension for rc/sc/prc, a
derived-and-verified signed delta formula, and the panel rewrite.

One thing worth flagging explicitly: the design doc's own suggested starting formula (`sc/prc -
rc/prc`) had the sign backwards for "positive = scale-up pressure." Caught by reading the saturation
engine's actual Go source before trusting the suggestion, per the spec's own instruction not to take
the formula as given. Used `rc/prc - sc/prc` instead, hand-verified against 2 real controller.log
ticks with independently known scale-up/scale-down outcomes.

Also applied the panel-3 legend-density lesson from fix-round 1 proactively here -- placed the
reason-marker key inside the axes from the start rather than below it, though even that first
attempt (a different corner) still needed one adjustment after viewing the render. Full detail in
`session/status/autoscaling-viz.md`, rewritten in place, prior entries preserved below the fold.

A fresh `review__autoscaling-viz-panel6-redesign-ready.md` trigger is filed for `/code-review`.

